Z||000000||mrgone||06-11-2001||03:03 PM||||ok my finish looks a bit dull, it looks like an original colour and may be the original paint. <P>i have clearcoat polish, coconut flavoured car wash (MMMM), back to black, and im going to get a claybar....<P>what steps does my ...flatness have to go through to get shiney. ||||reg||2
Z||000001||Ken Wittlief||06-11-2001||03:23 PM||||if you spray it with clear coat it will become glossy paint.<P>  most waxes, if applied to flat paint, will look like white bird fouling - dont wax flat paint unless you clear coat it first.||||reg||1
Z||000002||PBJ||06-11-2001||06:15 PM||||I would try getting the car's paint buffed or take it to a pro to look at it and get there free opinion.  I took mine and they said I would be wasting my money-it needed paint. And still needs paint.  $$<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GTPete.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jncomutt||06-11-2001||06:24 PM||||Try the "Meguires" system.  They have a body scrub.  Then use 1) cleaner  2) polish 3) wax<P>They sell the system by #s... If you get the body scrub, then do the 3 steps, it works Great!  Brought the life back on my 84.. Looks brand new!<P>------------------<BR>17 year old Fierophile<BR>'86 Coupe 160k miles<BR>'84 Mint Beauty 51k and original tires!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ken Wittlief||06-12-2001||09:49 AM||||oh wait, I though you were talking about the flat black paint on your car - looks like you are talking about the body paint. (your subject line threw me off, 'FLAT paint!'<P>   is it only dull, or does it look whiteish? is the clear coat peeling off?<P>  if its not too far gone you can buff the clear coat that is on there back up so it shines again, or have someone do it for you (using a power buffer and paint polish).<p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 06-12-2001).]||||reg||1
