Z||000006||mrgone||06-12-2001||12:57 PM||||no peeling<BR>a few chips and such though||||reg||1
Z||000007||Ken Wittlief||06-12-2001||01:42 PM||||is the clear coat polish a liquid stuff or is it a wax like 'oxidation remover'?<P>  I would get a can of turtle wax polish and scratch remover - looks like paste wax, comes in a green can, pick a small spot and give it a shot with a soft cloth - rub it on by hand. <P>  if the clear coat on the car is already bad, you cant ruin it, so might as well take a shot at it. If the turtle wax brings the shine back out, then you can get swirl remover and buff it up nice with a buffer.<P>  or like the other guy said, if you dont feel confident doing it yourself, take it to a paint shop or auto detailer and ask them if they think it can be buffed out.<P>  it sounds silly, but a glossy sparkely shine really makes a difference in the way a car looks, esp at night under the lights.||||reg||1
Z||000008||mrgone||06-12-2001||02:03 PM||||yeah, its a tuna can of hard turtle wax clear coat polish||||reg||1
